# Feature: Task allocation (automatic & manual)

## Automatic mode
1. User selects an active `WorkflowPattern` (optionally scoped to product type).
2. System reads every `WorkflowPatternTask` row and creates one `DesignTask`
   per row, resolving `RoleId`/`SkillId` to an eligible employee.
3. `PlannedStart` / `DueAt` are computed from each row's `DayOffset` and the
   design's start date.

### Reference pattern (for tests / seed data)
| Seq | Sub-process | Default role | Hours | Day offset | Priority |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | Concept Review | Design Head | 2 | 0 | High |
| 2 | Sketch Creation | Sketch Designer | 8 | 1 | High |
| 3 | Sketch Approval | Design Head | 2 | 2 | High |
| 4 | Punching / Wilcom | Punching Designer | 12 | 3 | High |
| 5 | Machine Sample | Machine Operator | 6 | 5 | Medium |
| 6 | Sample Checking | Checker | 3 | 6 | High |
| 7 | Costing | Costing Team | 2 | 7 | Medium |
| 8 | Final Approval | Design Head | 2 | 8 | High |

## Manual mode
- Minimum one task row required.
- Each row: ProcessId, SubProcessId, AssignedEmployeeId/RoleId,
  ExpectedMinutes, PlannedStart, DueAt, Priority, dependency/sequence.
- Rows can be inserted, deleted, and reordered before save.
- The same sub-process may appear more than once (e.g. "Sketch Correction V2").
- **Never** silently replace manual tasks with workflow defaults on save.

## API
- `POST /api/designs/{id}/tasks/generate` - generate from a workflow pattern.
- `POST /api/tasks` - manual task create.
